* fpdummy.a - no-op floating-point startup, for programs that do not use FP.
*
* crt0/cstart unconditionally call _fpinit / _fpterm; this is the default that
* satisfies those calls for a program that doesn't opt in to floating point, so
* it neither links the MC6839 FPO9 module nor requires it to be present.  A
* program that uses FP links fpinit.a's object instead (host: fpinit.o, via
* c3lw -f or c3-ld -l=...fp.l; OS-9: -l=/dd/lib/fp.l ahead of clib.l).
 psect fpdummy_a,0,0,0,0,0

_fpinit:
 rts

_fpterm:
 rts

 endsect
